{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFTFhzeZ1X3J6ne6j3uV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated both files and changed nothing else. The JSON block is valid and the \"Recognition cues\" section is 40 lines (limit 60).\n\n1. **`reference/techniques/web.md`** (122 lines): I added day-by-day entries for the three day-21 challenges. D06 \"Reflect Upon This\" was reflected XSS: the server accepts the \"callback\" when your request carries browser fetch headers and a Referer from the reflected page, so no real browser is needed. D07 \"Stored for Later\" was stored XSS run by a real moderator bot; the proof shows up later on the entry page as a receipt. D08 \"Session Impression\" was session fixation: `?sid=<session_hint>`, then the cookie `arena_session=<hint>`. Each entry has the exact requests, the `effect`/error spellings, the times to CORRECT (78–116 s) and what went wrong in the timed modes. I compressed D01–D05 and added a section on the shared `/api/clues` layout that every app has used since D05.\n2. **Variant axes and pitfalls:** new axes for clue route words (`callback`/`internal`/`status`) and board nouns (`messages`/`postcards`), both covered by one rule: pick routes by clue key or `openapi.json`, never by the word in the value. New pitfalls cover solvers that call each other's `fallback()` and loop forever, apps slowing down when every probe hits them at once, too-short polling for the bot's receipt, and a submit that returned 503 even though the GM had recorded CORRECT.\n3. **`reference/coverage/web.md`:** reflected XSS, stored XSS and session fixation are marked seen and dropped from the gaps. I split the XSS/CSRF rows into DOM XSS, CSRF, open redirect, CORS and clickjacking, and added a session-hijack row. Priority 1 now goes to CSRF and DOM XSS (the bot is proven to exist), JWT and role tampering, open redirect, command injection, SSTI and SSRF. New gaps include `clue-json-router` (P1), `csrf-bot-planner`, `dom-xss-sink-scan` and a note about the 503/`already_solved` stop-gate problem. 25 prebuild gaps are queued, none built.\n\nThe web lane still can't be prebuilt: `hctf/prebuild.py` has no `web` entry and `lib/web.py` doesn't exist, so none of these gaps will drain until someone who owns `hctf/` adds them. That is still the top note in the gaps list."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":97833,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3fb4241-89d3-40ca-9929-a75c6d380cfd","uuid":"56f5ec9b-ea17-4c96-a0d3-c8176748aaec","timestamp":"2026-10-21T13:22:38.466Z","request_id":"req_011CgFTFhVPZ27a5sThDVUPH"}
